# Local AIDE exclusions for Docker homelab.
# Named 98_* so it loads before 99_aide_root's "/ Full" catch-all, and deployed WITHOUT a dot:
# aide.conf only includes conf.d names matching ^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$
# (hosts/components/integrity-scans/component.yml).
# AIDE uses first-match-wins, so these exclusions take precedence.

# Docker image layers and overlay2 filesystem — change on every pull/deploy
!/var/lib/docker/

# Container application data — media, downloads, app databases (high-churn)
!/home/{{ sys_user }}/server/containers/data/

# k3s workload data, the cluster nodes' counterpart of the Docker paths above. Each changes on
# every write, pull or pod start, so AIDE would hash it weekly and report it every week. The
# root filesystem it sits on held 469 GB on daniel-box on 2026-10-12. The k3s binaries
# (/var/lib/rancher/k3s/data), its certificates and staged manifests (the rest of
# /var/lib/rancher/k3s/server) and /etc/rancher stay checked. Absent on daniel-pi; a rule for a
# missing path matches nothing.
# Longhorn replica images: every volume's block data
!/var/lib/longhorn/
# containerd image layers and container snapshots
!/var/lib/rancher/k3s/agent/containerd/
# The same container filesystems again, mounted: containerd mounts every running container's
# root filesystem as an overlay under its runtime state directory, so the snapshot exclusion
# above does not keep AIDE out of them. daniel-box held 176 such mounts on 2026-10-20, and the
# 2026-10-19 scan was still hashing files inside them 35 hours in (#5785). The Pi's Docker
# containerd keeps its runtime state under /run/containerd.
!/run/k3s/
!/run/containerd/
# Network namespace handles, one per pod: nsfs mounts, not files
!/run/netns/
# The embedded etcd's data and its local snapshots
!/var/lib/rancher/k3s/server/db/
# Pod volumes: emptyDirs and projected Secrets and ConfigMaps
!/var/lib/kubelet/pods/
# CSI volume mounts (the Longhorn driver stages every attached volume's filesystem here, so this
# is live application data) and kubelet's own state files, rewritten on every pod change. 30 of
# daniel-server's 53 aideinit warnings on 2026-10-20 (#5794).
!/var/lib/kubelet/plugins/
!/var/lib/kubelet/[a-z_]+_state$
# Container logs
!/var/log/pods/
!/var/log/containers/

# Claude Code worktrees: each is a full checkout of this repo with its own .venv, created and
# removed by agent sessions every day. On 2026-10-20 daniel-box held 83 of them, 2.19M of the
# 5.1M inodes on its root filesystem, and the weekly check ran 35 hours without finishing
# (#5785). The primary checkout beside them stays checked.
!/home/{{ sys_user }}/server/\.claude/worktrees/

# Per-user caches and session state: package-manager download caches (uv, prek, npm) and
# per-session review scratch, all rewritten by ordinary use. ~/.local/share stays checked,
# because the uv-managed Pythons, uv tools and node versions there are executables.
!/home/[^/]+/\.cache/
!/home/[^/]+/\.kube/cache/
!/home/[^/]+/\.npm/
!/home/[^/]+/\.local/state/

# The media library: 432 GB on daniel-box's root filesystem on 2026-10-20, under
# fake_remux_host_data_root. Every file there gets AIDE's Full rule (about ten digests), which
# kept the 2026-10-20 aideinit on daniel-box running past an hour where daniel-server, without
# a library, finished in 28 minutes. Video files carry nothing an integrity check protects, and
# the *arr stack replaces them routinely.
!/srv/media/
# Swap files: rewritten by the kernel continuously, 8 GB each on the cluster nodes.
!/swap\.img$
!/swapfile$

# vfat has no stored inode numbers. The kernel invents one each time it loads a file's inode,
# so the number changes across a mount and also within one, once the inode leaves the cache.
# Every vfat path therefore gets Full-i, the rule the aide package's 31_aide_grub-efi gives
# Debian's EFI/debian.
# The EFI loaders Ubuntu installs: the 2026-11-09 check on daniel-box paged on seven of these
# with their 2026-07-31 mtimes intact. EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI, the one file 31_aide_grub-efi
# covers, did not page.
/boot/efi/EFI/(ubuntu|BOOT)$ d Full-i
/boot/efi/EFI/(ubuntu|BOOT)/[^/]+$ f Full-i
# The Pi's firmware partition: the 2026-11-10 check on daniel-pi paged on 734 of its files,
# whose only change was the inode, three hours after a baseline taken on the same boot.
/boot/firmware(/|$) Full-i

# Virtual/pseudo filesystems — not real files, cause inflated read counts
!/proc/
!/sys/
{% if integrity_scans_aide_lean | bool %}

# A 456 MB host. Debian's Full keeps about eleven digests per entry, and AIDE holds every entry
# in memory: the 2026-11-12 scan on daniel-pi swapped to the SD card until the watchdog's
# max-load-1 reset the board. sha256 alone measured 30% less memory and 85% less CPU per entry.
# The kernel headers are a third of the Pi's entries, and nothing on the Pi executes them.
HomelabLean = InodeData+m+c+sha256
!/usr/src(/|$)
# Placed before 99_aide_root's `/ 0 Full`, so it is the root rule that wins.
/ HomelabLean
{% endif %}
